# Keep it clean

One Dollar Computer should feel calm and obvious. Prefer fewer controls over more features.

## Do

- One primary action per surface (e.g. Upload, Sign in)
- Short labels: **Sign in**, **Sign out**, **/cloud** — never "Sign in Account", "Your account", or stacked synonyms
- Hide advanced tools until they are needed (owner-only, after sign-in, after first edit)
- When in doubt, leave it out or put it behind an existing menu

## Don’t

- Add badges, chips, dual CTAs, or redundant nav for the same job
- Invent settings panels, dashboards, or "power user" chrome unless explicitly asked
- Show both guest and signed-in chrome at once
- Expand copy: one sentence beats a paragraph of explanation

## Check before shipping

If a new control can be removed and the user still completes the task, remove it.
